  "id": "DrugBank_DB00352 - MONDO_15667",
  "verbalization": "Tioguanine is linked to Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia through a series of indication pathways, with Mitoxantrone acting as a common intermediate in all three paths. The evidence suggests that Tioguanine may be associated with a broader class of myeloid leukemias, including Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia and Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation, all of which are classified under the broader category of Acute Myeloid Leukemia. The shared indication to Mitoxantrone implies a potential mechanistic link, though the exact nature of this relationship remains unclear. The presence of multiple pathways with similar scores suggests that Tioguanine may have a role in the treatment or pathogenesis of this leukemia subtype, though further investigation is needed to clarify the precise mechanism of action.",
